Writeup/writeup_files/figure-latex/

# ── Large probe artifacts: kept locally, not tracked ─────────────────────────
# ~16.5 GB of layer embeddings and ~644 MB of compressed probe predictions.
# Both are regenerable from the pipeline that IS tracked:
#   Scripts/pipeline/extract_embeddings.py  -> Data/**/layer_{N}.npz
#   Scripts/pipeline/by_layer_mlp.py        -> Results/{slug}/by_layer_corpus_pred.csv.xz
# The small summaries the paper actually renders from stay tracked
# (Data/brms_relfreq_prop.rds, Data/relfreq_slope_curve.csv,
#  Results/{slug}/by_layer_mlp.csv), so the writeup builds from a clean clone.
*.npz
*.csv.xz
*.xz
